   "evidence": "`FiniteField.lean:52` `@[simp] qPowerFrobeniusTwistIso_hom : ... .hom = pullback.fst _ _` is the only simp lemma for this isomorphism. The PR adds `qPowerFrobeniusTwistBaseChangeIso_inv_fst/_inv_snd` (lines 113\u2013129) for the other isomorphism but no inverse lemma for this one.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/Frobenius/FiniteField.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[reassoc (attr := simp)] qPowerFrobeniusTwistIso_inv_fst : (f.qPowerFrobeniusTwistIso p a ha).inv \u226b pullback.fst _ _ = \ud835\udfd9 X` and `@[reassoc (attr := simp)] qPowerFrobeniusTwistIso_inv_snd : (f.qPowerFrobeniusTwistIso p a ha).inv \u226b pullback.snd _ _ = f`.",
   "issue": "`qPowerFrobeniusTwistIso` only has lemmas for its forward map (`_hom`, `_hom_comp`). It has no inverse projection lemmas, and once `_hom` rewrites `.hom` to `pullback.fst _ _`, simp can no longer close `e.inv \u226b pullback.fst _ _ = \ud835\udfd9 X` or `e.inv \u226b pullback.snd _ _ = f`. That leaves the map `X \u27f6` twist with no usable API, unlike the base-change isomorphism, which gets `_inv_fst` and `_inv_snd` in this same PR.",
   "line": 52
  }
 ],
